@lang en
IMPORT `bmcar-nouns`

-- Named cases for the tests (bmcar-tests.l4) and the findings (bmcar-findings.l4). No
-- directive is in this module; it holds facts only.
--
-- Every figure here is HYPOTHETICAL: the document prints no sum, limit, deductible or
-- premium, so each is a Schedule figure invented for the case, in VND, chosen to make the
-- arithmetic visible. The dates are 2026-2027. The full record literals for `A loss to an
-- item` and `A claim under Section II` are written by scratchpad/vn22/gen_fixtures.py from
-- one set of defaults plus each fixture's stated differences (L4 has no record update);
-- the script computes no expected value.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `Items and Schedules`

`item 1, the contract works`               MEANS `An item entered in the Schedule` WITH `item number` IS 1, `description` IS "the contract works", `sum insured` IS 10_000_000_000
`item 2, construction plant`               MEANS `An item entered in the Schedule` WITH `item number` IS 2, `description` IS "construction plant and equipment", `sum insured` IS 2_000_000_000
`item 3, construction machinery`           MEANS `An item entered in the Schedule` WITH `item number` IS 3, `description` IS "construction machinery", `sum insured` IS 1_000_000_000
`item 4, site offices`                     MEANS `An item entered in the Schedule` WITH `item number` IS 4, `description` IS "site offices", `sum insured` IS 500_000_000
`an item not in the Schedule`              MEANS `An item entered in the Schedule` WITH `item number` IS 5, `description` IS "a crane hired after inception", `sum insured` IS 300_000_000
`item 2, plant insured at its actual value` MEANS `An item entered in the Schedule` WITH `item number` IS 2, `description` IS "construction plant and equipment", `sum insured` IS 1_200_000_000

`the contract value of the works at completion is 10 billion` MEANS
    `The full contract value of the works at completion` WITH
        `the contract value at completion, with all materials, wages, freight, customs duties and other taxes` IS 10_000_000_000
        `the value of materials or items supplied by the principal`                                         IS 0

-- Period 1 March 2026 to 28 February 2027; Section I total 13.5 billion, debris 200
-- million, deductible 50 million; Section II limit 5 billion, deductible 20 million.
GIVEN lim IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      deb IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      its IS A LIST OF `An item entered in the Schedule`
GIVETH A `The Schedule`
`a Schedule with per-occurrence limit` lim `debris sum` deb `and items` its MEANS
    `The Schedule` WITH
        `the premium stated in the Schedule`                            IS 120_000_000
        `the date the Schedule states the insurance begins`             IS YMD 2026 3 1
        `the date the Schedule states the insurance ends`               IS YMD 2027 2 28
        `the items entered in the Schedule`                             IS its
        `the total sum insured under Section I`                         IS 13_500_000_000
        `the limit of indemnity for any one occurrence under Section I` IS lim
        `the separate sum for clearance of debris`                      IS deb
        `the deductible under Section I for each occurrence`            IS 50_000_000
        `the limit of indemnity under Section II`                       IS 5_000_000_000
        `the deductible under Section II for each occurrence`           IS 20_000_000

`the four items` MEANS LIST `item 1, the contract works`, `item 2, construction plant`, `item 3, construction machinery`, `item 4, site offices`

`the Schedule`                                        MEANS `a Schedule with per-occurrence limit` NOTHING             `debris sum` (JUST 200_000_000) `and items` `the four items`
`the Schedule with a per-occurrence limit of 300 million` MEANS `a Schedule with per-occurrence limit` (JUST 300_000_000) `debris sum` (JUST 200_000_000) `and items` `the four items`
`the Schedule with a per-occurrence limit of 1.5 billion` MEANS `a Schedule with per-occurrence limit` (JUST 1_500_000_000) `debris sum` (JUST 200_000_000) `and items` `the four items`
`the Schedule with no sum for debris`                 MEANS `a Schedule with per-occurrence limit` NOTHING             `debris sum` NOTHING            `and items` `the four items`
`the Schedule with plant insured at its actual value` MEANS `a Schedule with per-occurrence limit` NOTHING             `debris sum` (JUST 200_000_000) `and items` (LIST `item 1, the contract works`, `item 2, plant insured at its actual value`)

§§ `Policies`

GIVEN s    IS A `The Schedule`
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
      wc   IS A MAYBE DATE
      ul   IS A MAYBE DATE
      ext  IS A MAYBE DATE
      ot   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The policy in force`
`a policy on` s `premium paid` paid `works commenced` wc `unloaded` ul `extended to` ext `overtime agreed` ot MEANS
    `The policy in force` WITH
        `the Schedule`                                                                      IS s
        `the premium has been paid`                                                         IS paid
        `the date work on the site commenced`                                               IS wc
        `the date the items entered in the Schedule were unloaded at the site`              IS ul
        `the end date of an extension agreed by Bao Minh in writing`                        IS ext
        `overtime, night work, holiday work and express freight were agreed in writing in advance` IS ot

-- Plant unloaded on 5 March 2026, works commenced on 10 March 2026, premium paid.
`the policy`                                   MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule` `premium paid` TRUE  `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `unloaded` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)) `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` FALSE
`the policy with the premium unpaid`           MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule` `premium paid` FALSE `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `unloaded` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)) `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` FALSE
`the policy before any work or unloading`      MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule` `premium paid` TRUE  `works commenced` NOTHING                `unloaded` NOTHING               `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` FALSE
`the policy where work began before the Schedule date` MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule` `premium paid` TRUE `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 15)) `unloaded` NOTHING `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` FALSE
`the policy extended in writing to 31 May 2027` MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule` `premium paid` TRUE  `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `unloaded` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)) `extended to` (JUST (YMD 2027 5 31)) `overtime agreed` FALSE
`the policy with overtime agreed`              MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule` `premium paid` TRUE  `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `unloaded` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)) `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` TRUE
`the policy with a per-occurrence limit of 300 million` MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule with a per-occurrence limit of 300 million` `premium paid` TRUE `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `unloaded` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)) `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` FALSE
`the policy with a per-occurrence limit of 1.5 billion` MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule with a per-occurrence limit of 1.5 billion` `premium paid` TRUE `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `unloaded` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)) `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` FALSE
`the policy with no sum for debris`            MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule with no sum for debris` `premium paid` TRUE `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `unloaded` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)) `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` FALSE
`the policy with plant insured at its actual value` MEANS `a policy on` `the Schedule with plant insured at its actual value` `premium paid` TRUE `works commenced` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `unloaded` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 5)) `extended to` NOTHING `overtime agreed` FALSE

§§ `The Insured's conduct of the risk`

GIVEN ans  IS A BOOLEAN
      prec IS A BOOLEAN
      info IS A BOOLEAN
      chg  IS A BOOLEAN
      ntf  IS A BOOLEAN
      prov IS A BOOLEAN
      unap IS A BOOLEAN
      subr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Insured's conduct of the risk`
`conduct of the risk with answers true` ans `precautions` prec `information` info `material change` chg `notified` ntf `provided for` prov `unapproved change` unap `subrogation` subr MEANS
    `The Insured's conduct of the risk` WITH
        `the answers in the questionnaire and the proposal were true`                       IS ans
        `took every reasonable precaution and followed Bao Minh's reasonable recommendations` IS prec
        `complied with the regulations and the manufacturer's recommendations`              IS prec
        `gave Bao Minh's representatives the details and information needed to assess the risk` IS info
        `there was a material change in the risk`                                           IS chg
        `notified the material change immediately, by telegram and in writing`              IS ntf
        `took the additional precautions the change required`                               IS prov
        `made or admitted a material change increasing the risk without Bao Minh's written approval` IS unap
        `did and permitted the acts Bao Minh required to enforce rights against third parties` IS subr

`proper conduct of the risk`                                MEANS `conduct of the risk with answers true` TRUE  `precautions` TRUE  `information` TRUE `material change` FALSE `notified` FALSE `provided for` FALSE `unapproved change` FALSE `subrogation` TRUE
`conduct of the risk after an untrue answer`                MEANS `conduct of the risk with answers true` FALSE `precautions` TRUE  `information` TRUE `material change` FALSE `notified` FALSE `provided for` FALSE `unapproved change` FALSE `subrogation` TRUE
`conduct of the risk without reasonable precautions`        MEANS `conduct of the risk with answers true` TRUE  `precautions` FALSE `information` TRUE `material change` FALSE `notified` FALSE `provided for` FALSE `unapproved change` FALSE `subrogation` TRUE
`conduct of the risk withholding information`               MEANS `conduct of the risk with answers true` TRUE  `precautions` TRUE  `information` FALSE `material change` FALSE `notified` FALSE `provided for` FALSE `unapproved change` FALSE `subrogation` TRUE
`conduct of the risk with a change notified by telegram and in writing` MEANS `conduct of the risk with answers true` TRUE `precautions` TRUE `information` TRUE `material change` TRUE `notified` TRUE `provided for` TRUE `unapproved change` FALSE `subrogation` TRUE
`conduct of the risk with a change notified in writing only` MEANS `conduct of the risk with answers true` TRUE  `precautions` TRUE  `information` TRUE `material change` TRUE  `notified` FALSE `provided for` TRUE  `unapproved change` FALSE `subrogation` TRUE
`conduct of the risk with an unapproved change increasing the risk` MEANS `conduct of the risk with answers true` TRUE `precautions` TRUE `information` TRUE `material change` TRUE `notified` TRUE `provided for` TRUE `unapproved change` TRUE `subrogation` TRUE
`conduct of the risk refusing help with subrogation`        MEANS `conduct of the risk with answers true` TRUE  `precautions` TRUE  `information` TRUE `material change` FALSE `notified` FALSE `provided for` FALSE `unapproved change` FALSE `subrogation` FALSE

§§ `Notices and the Insured's conduct after an occurrence`

GIVEN rcv IS A MAYBE DATE
      imm IS A BOOLEAN
      tel IS A BOOLEAN
      wri IS A BOOLEAN
      sta IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The notice of an occurrence`
`a notice received` rcv `immediately` imm `by phone or telegram` tel `in writing` wri `stating nature and extent` sta MEANS
    `The notice of an occurrence` WITH
        `the date Bao Minh received the notice`     IS rcv
        `given immediately`                         IS imm
        `by telephone or telegram`                  IS tel
        `in writing`                                IS wri
        `stating the nature and extent of the loss` IS sta

GIVEN n   IS A `The notice of an occurrence`
      mni IS A BOOLEAN
      prs IS A BOOLEAN
      inf IS A BOOLEAN
      pol IS A BOOLEAN
      rep IS A BOOLEAN
      adm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Insured's conduct after the occurrence`
`conduct after notice` n `minimised` mni `preserved` prs `informed` inf `police` pol `repaired early` rep `admitted` adm MEANS
    `The Insured's conduct after the occurrence` WITH
        `the notice`                                                                      IS n
        `took all steps within its power to minimise the loss`                            IS mni
        `preserved the damaged parts and made them available for inspection`             IS prs
        `furnished the information and documents Bao Minh required`                       IS inf
        `informed the police`                                                             IS pol
        `repaired, before an inspection, damage that was not minor`                       IS rep
        `made an admission, offer, promise or payment without Bao Minh's written consent` IS adm

-- The occurrence of 10 June 2026: notice received on 13 June, by telephone and in writing.
`a proper notice received on 13 June 2026` MEANS `a notice received` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 13)) `immediately` TRUE `by phone or telegram` TRUE `in writing` TRUE `stating nature and extent` TRUE

`the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` `a proper notice received on 13 June 2026` `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, police informed` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` `a proper notice received on 13 June 2026` `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` TRUE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice received on 24 June` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` (`a notice received` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 24)) `immediately` TRUE `by phone or telegram` TRUE `in writing` TRUE `stating nature and extent` TRUE) `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice received on 25 June` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` (`a notice received` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 25)) `immediately` TRUE `by phone or telegram` TRUE `in writing` TRUE `stating nature and extent` TRUE) `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice in writing only` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` (`a notice received` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 13)) `immediately` TRUE `by phone or telegram` FALSE `in writing` TRUE `stating nature and extent` TRUE) `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, notice on day 2 not immediate` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` (`a notice received` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 12)) `immediately` FALSE `by phone or telegram` TRUE `in writing` TRUE `stating nature and extent` TRUE) `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, no notice` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` (`a notice received` NOTHING `immediately` FALSE `by phone or telegram` FALSE `in writing` FALSE `stating nature and extent` FALSE) `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, with an early repair` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` `a proper notice received on 13 June 2026` `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` TRUE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, loss not minimised` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` `a proper notice received on 13 June 2026` `minimised` FALSE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` FALSE
`the Insured's conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026, with an admission of liability` MEANS
    `conduct after notice` `a proper notice received on 13 June 2026` `minimised` TRUE `preserved` TRUE `informed` TRUE `police` FALSE `repaired early` FALSE `admitted` TRUE

§§ `Claim histories`

GIVEN frd IS A BOOLEAN
      fls IS A BOOLEAN
      fmn IS A BOOLEAN
      rej IS A BOOLEAN
      awd IS A MAYBE `An arbitral award`
      prc IS A MAYBE DATE
      ast IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The history of a claim`
`a claim history, fraudulent` frd `false declaration` fls `fraudulent means` fmn `rejected` rej `award` awd `proceedings` prc `as at` ast MEANS
    `The history of a claim` WITH
        `the claim is fraudulent`                                                   IS frd
        `a false declaration was made or used in support of the claim`              IS fls
        `fraudulent means or devices were used by or for the Insured to obtain a benefit` IS fmn
        `the claim was rejected`                                                    IS rej
        `the award`                                                                 IS awd
        `the date proceedings were commenced`                                       IS prc
        `as at`                                                                     IS ast

`the award of the two arbitrators on 30 September 2026` MEANS `An arbitral award` WITH `made by` IS `the two arbitrators`, `the date of the award` IS YMD 2026 9 30
`the award of a single arbitrator on 30 September 2026` MEANS `An arbitral award` WITH `made by` IS `a single arbitrator appointed by both parties`, `the date of the award` IS YMD 2026 9 30

`a clean claim history`               MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` FALSE `award` NOTHING `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2026 12 31)
`a fraudulent claim history`          MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` TRUE  `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` FALSE `award` NOTHING `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2026 12 31)
`a history with a false declaration`  MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` TRUE  `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` FALSE `award` NOTHING `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2026 12 31)
`a history with fraudulent means`     MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` TRUE `rejected` FALSE `award` NOTHING `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2026 12 31)
`rejected, award of 30 September 2026, no proceedings, as at 30 December 2026` MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` TRUE `award` (JUST `the award of the two arbitrators on 30 September 2026`) `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2026 12 30)
`rejected, award of 30 September 2026, no proceedings, as at 31 December 2026` MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` TRUE `award` (JUST `the award of the two arbitrators on 30 September 2026`) `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2026 12 31)
`rejected, award of 30 September 2026, proceedings on 30 December 2026` MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` TRUE `award` (JUST `the award of the two arbitrators on 30 September 2026`) `proceedings` (JUST (YMD 2026 12 30)) `as at` (YMD 2027 6 30)
`rejected, award of 30 September 2026, proceedings on 31 December 2026` MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` TRUE `award` (JUST `the award of the two arbitrators on 30 September 2026`) `proceedings` (JUST (YMD 2026 12 31)) `as at` (YMD 2027 6 30)
`rejected, sole arbitrator's award of 30 September 2026, no proceedings, as at 31 December 2026` MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` TRUE `award` (JUST `the award of a single arbitrator on 30 September 2026`) `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2026 12 31)
`not rejected, award of 30 September 2026, no proceedings, as at 31 December 2026` MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` FALSE `award` (JUST `the award of the two arbitrators on 30 September 2026`) `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2026 12 31)
`rejected outright in 2026, no arbitration, no proceedings, as at 2031` MEANS `a claim history, fraudulent` FALSE `false declaration` FALSE `fraudulent means` FALSE `rejected` TRUE `award` NOTHING `proceedings` NOTHING `as at` (YMD 2031 1 1)

§§ `Losses to items (Section I)`

-- A storm damages the works; repair necessarily costs 400 million and that is what was spent.
`the standard loss to the works` MEANS `A loss to an item` WITH
    `the item`                                                                             IS `item 1, the contract works`
    `what the property is`                                                                 IS `the contract works or other property of an ordinary kind`
    `physical loss or damage`                                                              IS TRUE
    `sudden and unforeseen`                                                                IS TRUE
    `to an extent that requires repair or replacement`                                     IS TRUE
    `the causes`                                                                           IS LIST (`a cause the policy does not name, namely` "storm")
    `discovered only when an inventory was taken`                                          IS FALSE
    `the damaged part had been handed over before the occurrence`                          IS FALSE
    `the damaged part had been put into use before the occurrence`                         IS FALSE
    `damaged in an earlier occurrence and not then repaired properly without delay`        IS FALSE
    `the state after the occurrence`                                                       IS `repairable, at a necessary cost of` 400_000_000
    `the actual value immediately before the occurrence`                                   IS 6_000_000_000
    `the value of salvage`                                                                 IS 0
    `the cost the Insured has actually incurred in repairing or replacing it`              IS 400_000_000
    `of which, alterations, additions or improvements`                                     IS 0
    `of which, overtime, night work, holiday work or express freight`                      IS 0
    `of which, provisional repairs not part of the final repairs or increasing their cost` IS 0
    `of which, replacing, repairing or rectifying defective material or workmanship`       IS 0
    `the part of the loss not included in the sum insured`                                 IS 0
    `the invoices and documents showing the repair or replacement were produced`           IS TRUE
    `the full contract value of the works at completion`                                   IS JUST `the contract value of the works at completion is 10 billion`
    `the replacement value by a new item of the same kind and capacity`                    IS NOTHING

-- The same loss, to an item the Schedule does not list.
