      h   IS A `The history of a claim`
GIVETH A `A claim under Section I`
`a Section I claim on` d `for` ls `debris` dbr `consequential` csq `paid before` pdb `other insurance` oth `conduct` a `history` h MEANS
    `A claim under Section I` WITH
        `the date of the occurrence`                     IS d
        `the losses to items`                            IS ls
        `the cost of clearance of debris`                IS dbr
        `the consequential losses claimed`               IS csq
        `Section I indemnity already paid in the period` IS pdb
        `another insurance covers the same loss`         IS oth
        `the Insured's conduct after the occurrence`     IS a
        `the history of the claim`                       IS h

-- The common case: occurrence on 10 June 2026, no debris, nothing consequential, nothing
-- paid before, no other insurance, proper conduct, a clean history.
GIVEN ls IS A LIST OF `A loss to an item`
GIVETH A `A claim under Section I`
`a standard claim for` ls MEANS
    `a Section I claim on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `for` ls `debris` 0 `consequential` 0 `paid before` 0 `other insurance` FALSE `conduct` `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026` `history` `a clean claim history`

§§ `Section II claims`

-- Materials fall from the scaffold onto a neighbour's shopfront: damages 300 million, claimant's costs 20 million, consented costs 30 million.
`the standard third-party claim` MEANS `A claim under Section II` WITH
    `the date of the occurrence`                                 IS YMD 2026 6 10
    `what the third party suffered`                              IS `loss of or damage to property belonging to the third party`
    `accidental`                                                 IS TRUE
    `in direct connection with the construction or erection of the items insured under Section I` IS TRUE
    `on or in the immediate vicinity of the site`                IS TRUE
    `the causes`                                                 IS LIST (`a cause the policy does not name, namely` "materials falling from the scaffold")
    `the vibration and support exclusion has been varied by endorsement` IS FALSE
    `the injured person is an employee or worker of the contractor, the principal or a firm connected with the works, or of their family` IS FALSE
    `the property belongs to or is in the care, custody or control of the contractor, the principal, a firm connected with the works, or an employee or worker of one of them` IS FALSE
    `the liability arises from an agreement of the Insured to pay by way of indemnity or otherwise` IS FALSE
    `the liability would have attached in the absence of that agreement` IS FALSE
    `the Insured is legally liable to pay damages`               IS TRUE
    `the damages the Insured is legally liable to pay`           IS 300_000_000
    `of which, expenditure on doing, redoing, making good, repairing or replacing anything insured or insurable under Section I` IS 0
    `the claimant's costs and expenses of litigation recovered from the Insured` IS 20_000_000
    `costs and expenses incurred with the written consent of Bao Minh` IS 30_000_000
    `another insurance covers the same liability`                IS FALSE
    `the Insured's conduct after the occurrence`                 IS `the Insured's proper conduct after an occurrence on 10 June 2026`
    `the history of the claim`                                   IS `a clean claim history`

